# tests/flake-update, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating
# this directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST. Every assertion is about a run's RESULT, and dispatching a run
# is what a worker does with `curry` + `run-then`. `update` resolves to the
# built tool; `flake` is the fixture it re-locks (flake.nix alone, no lock).
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --worker1:@=worker.sh --update:@=DEEP-DEPS/flake-update --flake:@=flake
